    "description": "Metre-gauge 'Eastern Line'; the last metre gauge in Iraq",
    "notes": "The IRR 'Eastern Line', the last metre-gauge railway in Iraq; closed 1984-88.  [route] Baghdad -> Baquba -> Kirkuk -> Erbil, with a branch from Jalawla Junction to Khanaqin (toward the Iranian border), held as an off-line extra_station. Metre gauge (1,000 mm).",
    "history": "A metre-gauge (1,000 mm) line: the Baghdad-toward-Persia section was built in WWI and later diverted to Khanaqin, extended from Kingerban to Kirkuk in 1925, and Kirkuk to Erbil in 1949. A Tigris bridge at Baghdad (1950) finally linked the east- and west-bank metre-gauge systems.",
    "verification_status": "unverified",
